<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Declining force of selection with age" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The strength of selection on survival falls with age after reproduction begins, so senescence is an inevitable outcome of natural selection." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "s(a) = \\frac{\\partial r}{\\partial \\ln p_a} = \\frac{1}{T}\\sum_{x=a+1}^{\\infty} e^{-rx} l_x m_x, non-increasing in a" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: an age-structured population with fixed age-specific fertility and no growth or repair after maturity. Formal status: the formula for s(a) is proved. The inevitability claim is refuted as stated: Jones et al. (2013) found species with flat or declining mortality with age, consistent with life histories where fertility rises with size." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Compare age trajectories of mortality and fertility across many species with the trajectories that s(a) predicts from each species' own life table." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "W. D. Hamilton (1966) The moulding of senescence by natural selection" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-senescence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature12789> .
}
